  "corrections": [
    {
      "paragraph": 2,
      "issue": "The bracket otherwise-zero assertion needs the opposite-root exception; the root-segment assertion excludes parallel roots and zero."
    },
    {
      "paragraph": 4,
      "issue": "The compressed boundary-orbit proof needs justification; a separate reconstruction supplies it with ordered-operator, chamber, and rank-one inputs."
    },
    {
      "paragraph": 10,
      "issue": "Cyclicity alone does not prove irreducibility; complete reducibility is stated as a dependency."
    },
    {
      "paragraph": 11,
      "issue": "Nonconstant analytic matrix coefficients need not have nonzero first derivatives at the identity. A weight-projection proof repairs the inference."
    },
    {
      "paragraph": 14,
      "issue": "The unsimplified type-A fractions contain coefficient/range errors. Correct fractions are given, with the printed Pi_2 coefficient identified."
    },
    {
      "paragraph": 21,
      "issue": "The sum of three coefficients need only be an integer, not necessarily a multiple of three. The exact reflection-integrality conditions are stated."
    },
    {
      "paragraph": 26,
      "issue": "The third orbit-pattern row has one half of the total sum where one third is required. The printed value fails norm preservation."
    },
    {
      "paragraph": 27,
      "issue": "The expanded Pi_7 vector is retained; its inconsistent alternative expression in omega_0 is corrected."
    },
    {
      "paragraph": 35,
      "issue": "The printed p_1=-3m_3 must be p_1=-3m_2. Pi_2 itself is an immediate counterexample to the print."
    },
    {
      "paragraph": 24,
      "issue": "The third printed g6 boundary family has squared norm 74/9 rather than 6. Replacing its second coefficient 2 by 1 gives 700 orbit points; the other 20 are the distinct-index expressions 2(omega_i+omega_j+omega_k)+3 omega_0. Exact integer reflection closure gives all 720 boundary weights. These are editorial repairs, not silently changed source claims."
    }
  ],
